.TITLE "curl"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Transfers data from or to a server. It supports a wide range of __protocols__ including HTTP, HTTPS, FTP, and more, making it a versatile tool for web interactions.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**curl url**
Displays the content of a URL in the terminal.
> __url__ the target web address

**curl -O url**
Downloads the content of a URL and saves it to a file with the same name.
> __-O__ remote name flag

**curl -o filename url**
Downloads the content of a URL and saves it to a specified filename.
> __-o__ output file flag | __filename__ local file name

**curl -L url**
Follows any HTTP redirects encountered when requesting the URL.
> __-L__ follow location flag

**curl -I url**
Fetches only the HTTP headers from the specified URL.
> __-I__ head flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __curl__ command is an essential tool for testing APIs and automating web requests. Use the __-v__ flag to see the full request and response headers, which is invaluable for debugging connection issues.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/curl.html__
